{
  "attack_description": "The promoted KPI's 5-fold GroupKFold(family) naturally isolates the 2 largest of 17 families (stainless_steel n=1976, nickel_alloy n=1888, 53.1%% of the classified cohort) into their own solo folds and packs the remaining 15 families into only 3 folds, so the reported R2 is a SAMPLE-weighted (per-row) out-of-fold statistic dominated by whichever families are large. This re-runs the identical feature engineering, HistGBM model, and seed with true Leave-One-Family-Out (n_splits=n_families=17, one family held out per fold) and reports the FAMILY-weighted (unweighted per family) mean R2 alongside the sample-weighted OOF R2, to test whether the KPI's claimed 'generalizes across metallurgical families' capability holds broadly across families, not just in the row-weighted aggregate.",
